        "original_id": "779ce266-a4e3-59c3-8fed-214d7ae048a2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Radiohead, Easy Star All-Stars, SubAudible Hum\n- Products: \"No Surprises\", \"OK Computer\", Radiodread, \"Lucky\", \"In Time For Spring, On Came The Snow\"\n- Places: Oxfordshire, Bath, St Catherine's Court\n- Topics: album recording, single release, tribute albums, musical comparison, award nomination\n\nFacts:\n- Radiohead recorded most of \"OK Computer\" at St Catherine's Court in Oxfordshire and Bath between 1996 and early 1997, while the song \"Lucky\" had been recorded earlier in 1995.\n- Radiohead released \"OK Computer\" in 1997 as their third studio album.\n- \"No Surprises\" is a song by Radiohead, and it was released on 12 January 1998 as the third and final single from \"OK Computer\".\n- Easy Star All-Stars released Radiodread in 2006 as a tribute album covering Radiohead's \"OK Computer\" in reggae, ska, and dub styles.\n- SubAudible Hum have often been compared to Radiohead, have been active on the live circuit particularly in their home town, and have released three albums.\n- SubAudible Hum's album \"In Time For Spring, On Came The Snow\" was nominated for the J Award.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "eecc43ae-581d-5621-9bb7-00bbb45ad4c5",
        "text": "Page: No Surprises. Sentence: \"No Surprises\" is a song by the English alternative rock band Radiohead, released as the third and final single from their third studio album \"OK Computer\" (1997) on 12 January 1998.\nPage: OK Computer. Sentence: Other than the song \"Lucky\", which was recorded in 1995, Radiohead recorded the album in Oxfordshire and Bath between 1996 and early 1997, mostly in the historic mansion St Catherine's Court.\nPage: Radiodread. Sentence: Radiodread is a 2006 tribute album by the Easy Star All-Stars that covers Radiohead's 1997 album \"OK Computer\" in reggae, ska and dub styles.\nPage: SubAudible Hum. Sentence: Often compared to Radiohead they are active on the live circuit, particularly in their home town, they have released three albums, one of which was nominated for the J Award; \"In Time For Spring, On Came The Snow\".",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
